# E §10 readers-of, L §6.4 (tally 2.1.7 B2, issue #133; P64): a scenario's row of b that reads a makes b a
# reader of a at the first layer, and no scenario row prints as a node of its own: `b, c, c_sc`. 2.1.6's refcore
# printed `c, input, b, c_sc`. (T's G11 r_agent_s1.)
=== r_agent_s1_base.tally
model base
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source card "card"

input a: num

input b: num

input ld: date

def c: num = b + a at ld

ask r_a: readers-of a

ask r_b: readers-of b

ask v: c

version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  a = 3
  b = 4
  ld = 2026-06-01
=== r_agent_s1_sc.tally
scenario sc over base
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01
  note "x"

version sv
  cite card
  governs 2026-01-01..
  known 2026-01-01
  replace b = base.a * base.a "linked"

ask r_a2: readers-of a in sc

ask c_sc: c in sc
=== expect r_a2 r_a
r_a2: b, c, c_sc
r_a: c, v
